        "principle": "Knowledge is not derived from sensory experience by induction; it is created by conjecture and winnowed by criticism, and a genuinely good explanation is one that is hard to vary while still accounting for what it purports to account for, which is why good explanations reach far beyond the evidence that inspired them.",
