        "principle": "Two extended case studies, Carlos the emerging-markets trader and John the high-yield trader, show that the traders who dominate a given market cycle are often those whose style happens to fit that cycle's specific randomness, not the most skilled overall, and that naive Darwinism misapplies evolutionary fitness to short time horizons.",
