        "principle": "Probability began as the child of ancient skepticism, the view that certainty is unavailable and only degrees of belief are possible, and Taleb argues the best traders, like the philosopher Carneades arguing both sides of the same case, are those who can reverse a position without shame the moment new evidence appears, unlike most people who become emotionally married to their prior opinions.",
