        "principle": "Since large-scale prediction is unreliable, the practical response is not paralysis but a deliberate asymmetry: be a fool only in low-stakes matters, maximize your exposure to lucky accidents, and structure your bets, financial and otherwise, as a barbell of extreme safety plus small extreme-upside speculation rather than a single 'medium risk' position.",
